[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    14[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    15[0m:[38;5;10m[49m The public API is a single `void premultiply(cp_image_t *)`. There is no
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    16[0m:[38;5;10m[49m options struct, no flags word, no mode enum, no compile-time `#ifdef` branch,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    17[0m:[38;5;10m[49m no byte-order switch, no element-type switch. Consequently the configuration
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    18[0m:[38;5;10m[49m surface is entirely **input shape**, and there is nothing to cross with it.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    19[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    20[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ### Public entry points (complete set, including the lowest level)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    21[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    22[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | entry point | level | in table |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    23[0m:[38;5;10m[49m |---|---|---|
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    24[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `premultiply` | the only one; it *is* the lowest level | yes |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    25[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    26[0m:[38;5;10m[49m There are no convenience wrappers and no internal helpers (`static` functions):
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    27[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `premultiply` is simultaneously the highest- and lowest-level entry point.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    28[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    29[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ### Input shape axes the code branches on
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    30[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    31[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | axis | values the C distinguishes | why (source evidence) |
