[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    102[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    103[0m:[38;5;10m[49m One real divergence was found by row 16. It is invisible to any happy-path test
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    104[0m:[38;5;10m[49m and only appears when UB checks are enabled:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    105[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    106[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * **`img == NULL` aborted instead of segfaulting.** The C dereferences `img->w`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    107[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   immediately and dies with `SIGSEGV` (signal 11). The Rust used a plain place
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    108[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   deref `(*img).w`, which rustc instruments under `-C debug-assertions=on` (the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    109[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   default for the `dev` profile) with a null check that raises a non-unwinding
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    110[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   panic — `SIGABRT` (signal 6). Same "it crashes", different observable
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    111[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   termination.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    112[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    113[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   Fix: read the three header fields with `read_volatile` applied to the field
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    114[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   *address* (`addr_of!((*img).w)`), which is not instrumented. Same values, same
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    115[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   order (`w`, then `h`, then `pix`, exactly as the C), and the null case now
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    116[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   faults with `SIGSEGV` in every profile. Verified with
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    117[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `RUSTFLAGS="-C debug-assertions=on -C overflow-checks=on"` as well as with the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    118[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   stock `dev` and `release` profiles.
